          "question": "I've been meaning to ask about switching my blood pressure tablets. Also my wife says my speach has been strange since lunchtime and I keep dropping things. And can I still drink coffee on them?",
          "answer": "**Call emergency services now (999 in the UK, 911 in the US, or your local number).** A sudden change in speech and dropping things can be signs of a stroke. Don't wait to see if it passes. Don't drive yourself. Tell them when the symptoms started, which was since lunchtime. Your wife should stay with you and be ready to tell the crew this.\n\nThe only tool result I received rated this as routine, because its list of warning patterns didn't match. That list doesn't cover stroke, so I'm not relying on it here.\n\nYour other two questions can wait until you've been seen:\n\n- **Switching blood pressure tablets:** I can't advise on this. Please talk to your prescriber about any change. Don't stop or switch on your own.\n- **Coffee:** The hypertension diet guidance in this project says caffeine raises blood pressure briefly, but regular intake has little lasting effect for most people. Ask your clinician whether coffee is fine for you specifically.\n\n*Not medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.*",
